  partId: waste_management
  displayName: Waste Management System
  shortName: Waste System
  zone: 1
  order: 160
  keySpec: Compact universal waste system
  summary: The spacecraft toilet. Apollo crews used bags; Orion carries a proper
    compact commode in a cabin the size of a small van.
  whyItMatters: Without gravity, waste must be moved by airflow rather than falling.
    A fan pulls air through a filtered separator, and the system is held slightly
    below cabin pressure so air always flows inwards, never out.
  narration: {fileID: 0}
